  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "3d7e7d4c-3234-47bc-a200-031f91963395",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 940,
        "content": "## Build a dual-stage RAG chat assistant with Google Drive, Pinecone and Gemini\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow implements an enterprise-grade, dual-stage Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system with Pinecone vector stores and semantic caching. It operates in two synchronized pipelines:\n\n1. **Document Ingestion Pipeline (Top Track)**: Continuously monitors Google Drive for newly uploaded or modified knowledge documents (PDFs, plain text, and Markdown), downloads them, extracts textual content, generates 768-dimensional dense vector embeddings using local Ollama (`nomic-embed-text`), and indexes the documents into a primary Pinecone knowledge base with source metadata.\n2. **Semantic Cache & Conversational AI Pipeline (Bottom Track)**: Intercepts incoming user chat questions and performs an ultra-fast vector similarity lookup in a Pinecone Semantic Cache index (`rag-semantic-cache`). If a semantic match is found (score >= 0.88), the cached answer is returned immediately in under 100ms. On a cache miss, the query is seamlessly routed to an autonomous AI Agent powered by Google Gemini 1.5 Flash, conversational buffer memory, and a Pinecone Vector Store retrieval tool. The AI Agent's grounded response is delivered to the user and automatically indexed into the Pinecone Semantic Cache for future instant retrieval.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- **Google Drive**: Connect your Google Drive OAuth2 credentials and specify your target Knowledge Base folder ID in the `When File Updated in Drive` and `Search Drive Files` nodes.\n- **Pinecone Vector Database**: Create two Pinecone indexes with dimension `768` and metric `cosine`:\n  - `nomic-embed-text`: Stores document chunks and metadata for knowledge retrieval.\n  - `rag-semantic-cache`: Stores cached Q&A query vectors and answers.\n- **Local Ollama**: Ensure Ollama is running (`ollama pull nomic-embed-text`) and configure the Ollama Base URL in your credentials (e.g., `http://localhost:11434` or `http://host.docker.internal:11434`).\n- **Google Gemini API**: Connect your Google Gemini (PaLM) API credentials and select `models/gemini-1.5-flash` for the agent and tool language models.\n- **Test Workflow**: Use the `Manual Test Trigger` to test knowledge base ingestion, and the `On Chat Message Received` trigger to test chat inference and cache seeding.\n\n### Customization\n\n- Adjust the similarity threshold in `Check Cache Hit` (default: `0.88`) to balance cache precision and hit rate.\n- Modify the AI Agent's system message in `AI Query Response Agent` to enforce custom domain personas or formatting rules.\n- Add additional file format parsers (e.g., DOCX, HTML) in the ingestion pipeline as needed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
